.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- copy files using colon-path atomic names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE DEST
.br
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE
\&...
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path wrapper around
.BR cp (1).
It rewrites path arguments, creates missing parent directories for
destinations, then executes
.BR cp .
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7)
for
.BR BASE:LEAF
syntax.
.PP
When the destination is a directory, each source is placed at
.I DEST/LEAF
using the atomic name of the source.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ \-a a/b:c/d ../x
Runs
.B cp \-a a/b/c/d ../x/c/d
after creating
.BR ../x/c .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten
.B cp
command without executing it.
.PP
All other options are passed through to
.BR cp (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR colon-path (7),
.BR colon-mv (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
